NAME
       access, creat - test access, create a file

SYNOPSIS
       #include <unistd.h>
       #include <fcntl.h>

       int access(const char *path, int mode);
       int creat(const char *path, mode_t mode);

DESCRIPTION
       access checks PATH against F_OK, R_OK, W_OK and X_OK for the
       calling user. Deciding with access and then opening leaves a gap
       in which the answer can change, so where it matters, open the
       file and handle the failure instead.

       creat is open with O_CREAT|O_WRONLY|O_TRUNC.

RETURN VALUE
       0 or a descriptor, -1 with errno set.

ERRORS
       ENOENT   the path does not exist
       EACCES   the requested access is denied

SEE ALSO
       open(2), stat(2), chmod(2)
